From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 16:49:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] webservices: Honour an SSL transport security binding, from a
 security description or an SSL binding template.

WS_SECURITY_BINDING_TYPE is numbered from 1, as in the SDK; WS_SSL_TRANSPORT_SECURITY_BINDING and the certificate
credentials are declared.  An HTTP channel with an SSL transport binding gives its requests the certificate
failures to ignore and the client certificate, found in a store by subject name or thumbprint or asked of the
caller's callback, and its session the secure protocols not disallowed.  WsCreateServiceProxyFromTemplate builds
that binding from the policy description and the template, a property given in both being E_INVALIDARG.

As on Windows 11 build 29671, an SSL binding on a channel that is not HTTP is E_INVALIDARG, WsOpenChannel asks the
certificate callback for the endpoint address with no via, failing if it fails, and a service proxy's channel
does not ask before its first call.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

